# Cloudflare Pages caches aggressively at the edge, including the HTML entry
# point. When it does, a browser loading the canonical URL runs an old bundle
# while `curl "...?v=123"` looks fine — a new query string is a new cache key —
# so a deployed fix appears not to have deployed. That cost hours on another app
# in this fleet.
#
# The entry point is never stored. The hashed assets it points at are immutable
# by construction, and the RCU screenshots never change once extracted, so both
# can be cached hard — which matters here, because the screens are 16MB and a
# trainee tapping through them should pay for each one once.
#
# /derived is the exception, and is a separate directory for exactly this
# reason. Those files are NOT extracted artwork: they are generated from it
# (tools/radar_chart.py, tools/trough_masks.py), with whatever the app has
# learned to draw itself rubbed out, and they are regenerated whenever it
# learns to draw more. Their names do not change, so cached hard they would
# leave anyone who visited before looking at artwork with last month's values
# still painted on it. They revalidate instead — a 304 on every load, which
# costs a round trip and nothing else.
#
# They cannot simply be a second rule under /screens/*: Cloudflare CONCATENATES
# the values of every rule that matches, so that produced the self-contradicting
# "immutable, no-cache" rather than overriding it.

/
  Cache-Control: no-store

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-store

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/screens/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/derived/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/captured/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/masks/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
